@startuml DeploymentSecurityStack
!include ../themes/dark-theme.puml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

actor "Developer / Operator" as Dev
rectangle "GitHub Repository" as Repo
rectangle "GitHub-hosted CI\nlightweight validation only" as GitHubCI
rectangle "Approved Internal Runner\nJenkins / GitLab / Argo / platform pipeline" as InternalRunner
rectangle "Local Security Gate\n./scripts/security-check.sh" as LocalGate
rectangle "Artifact Registry" as Registry
rectangle "Production Deployment\nTLS + mTLS + secret manager" as Production
rectangle "Observability Stack\nPrometheus + Grafana + OTEL" as Observability
rectangle "PostgreSQL\nAudit + rate limits + app state" as DB
rectangle "Structured Security Logs\nJSON + correlation IDs" as Logs
rectangle "Policy & Review\nchange record + approvals" as Policy

Dev --> Repo
Repo --> GitHubCI : PR/branch validation
GitHubCI --> InternalRunner : no authoritative gate
InternalRunner --> LocalGate : run approved internal security gate
LocalGate --> Registry : image + scan evidence
Registry --> Production : deploy by immutable digest
Production --> Observability : metrics + trace data
Production --> Logs : auth, authz, mTLS, audit events
Production --> DB : migrations + audit + rate-limit data
Policy --> InternalRunner : signoff / rotation / emergency approvals
Policy --> Production : trust, retention, incident ownership

note right of InternalRunner
  Production enforcement lives here:
  OSV, Trivy, image digest verification,
  Flyway validation, TLS tests,
  secret rotation evidence, audit retention checks
end note

@enduml
